      "summary": "State Rep. Jamie Walsh issued a statement after his district office received a threatening email. He thanked law enforcement for responding and condemned political threats and intimidation. No details about the nature of the threat, suspects, or investigation status were provided.",
      "action_type": "statement",
      "topics": [
        "public_safety"
      ],
      "spin_flag": false
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Walsh Announces Literacy Grant for Northwest Area School District",
    "url": "https://repwalsh.com/News/39012/Press-Releases/Walsh-Announces-Literacy-Grant-for-Northwest-Area-School-District",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Walsh Announces Literacy Grant for Northwest Area School District\nOctober 28, 2026\nHARRISBURG – State Rep. Jamie Walsh (R-Luzerne) announced that Northwest Area School District has been awarded a $168,094 Pennsylvania Structured Literacy Grant to support its literacy curriculum.\n“This funding will help Northwest build upon the important literacy work already taking place in the district and provide students with additional opportunities to strengthen their reading, writing and comprehension skills,” said Walsh. “Effective literacy programming can help support students’ needs, build confidence and make sure every student has the foundation needed to succeed in school and beyond.”\nThe funding will help the district build the systems, instructional capacity and evidence-based resources necessary to meet structured literacy requirements.\nGrants may be used to support activities including:\n•\tPurchasing High-Quality Instructional Materials (HQIM) aligned to Structured Literacy and the Science of Reading.\n•\tAcquiring Pennsylvania Department of Education (PDE)-approved universal reading screening assessments for students in grades K-3.\n•\tSupporting educator participation in PDE-approved structured literacy professional development.\n•\tDeveloping local implementation plans that align curriculum, assessment, intervention and professional learning.\n•\tBuilding sustainable literacy systems through coaching, data-based decision making and Multi-Tiered System of Supports (MTSS-Reading).\n•\tStrengthening collaboration among district leaders, principals, literacy coaches and instructional staff to ensure consistent implementation across schools.\n“This is an important investment in the future of Northwest students,” said Walsh.\nRepresentative Jamie Walsh\n117th Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Tricia Lehman\n717.772.9840\ntlehman@pahousegop.com\nRepWalsh.com / Facebook.com/RepJamieWalsh\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "Northwest Area School District in Luzerne County received a $168,094 state grant for structured literacy programs. The grant can be used for instructional materials, reading assessments for K-3 students, teacher professional development, and building literacy support systems. State Rep. Jamie Walsh announced the award but did not award it himself — the grant comes from a Pennsylvania Department of Education program.",
      "action_type": "statement",
      "topics": [
        "education"
      ],
      "spin_flag": true
    }
  }
